DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: what a pneumatic valve does.
# Model: Pneumatic cylinder. Motor A turns the lever of a pneumatic valve. The valve takes
# its air from the tank on the left; two hoses run from its outlets to the two ends of a
# cylinder. Turn the lever one way and the air pushes the cylinder's rod out; turn it the
# other way and the rod goes back in. In the middle the valve is shut and the rod stays.
# Every stroke uses up some of the tank's air: watch "Air" under the picture fall.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor stop action A hold
  set motor speed A 20
  REPEAT 2:
    display text "out"
    run motor A counterclockwise 40 degrees
    wait 2 seconds
    display text "in"
    run motor A clockwise 80 degrees
    wait 2 seconds
    run motor A counterclockwise 40 degrees
  display text "shut"
  wait 1 seconds
